# tests/infra/run-all-skip-closures.manifest — per-member tracked-file closure
# for the content-addressed run_all.sh SKIP engine (task 5273, merge-gate-
# riders PRD §4 rider γ). Read ONLY by run_all.sh's skip engine (via the
# RUN_ALL_SKIP_CLOSURES_MANIFEST override) and by the under-declaration
# drift-guard in tests/infra/test_run_all_content_skip.sh.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ROW FORMAT
#   <test_basename> <path-or-glob> [<path-or-glob> ...]
#
# The listed paths are REPO-RELATIVE (scripts/foo.sh, tests/infra/bar.sh,
# gui/dist, .gitignore, ...). A glob (`scripts/*`, `gui/dist/*`) is matched
# by the skip engine as a git pathspec and by the drift-guard with `[[ ==  ]]`
# (where `*` spans `/`). Comment lines (^\s*#) and blank lines are ignored.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE COMPLETE closure (soundness INVERSION vs verify-pipeline-infra-tests.txt)
#   Each row must declare the member's *COMPLETE* tracked-file closure: every
#   tracked file whose content, if it changed, could change this member's
#   PASS/FAIL verdict. This is the exact INVERSE of the soundness direction
#   scripts/verify-pipeline-infra-tests.txt optimizes for: that manifest's
#   per-test sets are intentionally INCOMPLETE (sound for INCLUSION — "run at
#   least these" — but UNSOUND for SKIPPING, since a missing entry there just
#   over-runs, while a missing entry HERE would wrongly SKIP a member whose
#   real input changed). PRD §4.1. When unsure, DECLARE MORE (over-declaration
#   is sound — it only forces extra runs; under-declaration is the only bug).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SIX IMPLICIT closure members (appended to EVERY row by the engine — never
# list them here):
#   1. the member's own file            (<infra_dir>/<basename>)
#   2. tests/infra/test_helpers.sh      (shared assert/summary harness)
#   3. tests/infra/run_all.sh           (the runner itself)
#   4. tests/infra/run-all-classification-lib.sh
#   5. tests/infra/load_tolerance_lib.sh
#   6. the two harness manifests:
#         tests/infra/run-all-classification.manifest
#         tests/infra/run-all-ambient-vars.manifest
#   (paths are resolved relative to the invocation's infra dir, so hermetic
#   fixtures and the real merge both work — see run_all.sh's skip engine.)
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FAIL-OPEN
#   A member with NO row here is UNMAPPED and NEVER skips (the engine logs
#   `RUN (unmapped): <m>` and runs it). A missing/empty manifest degrades to
#   "every member unmapped" ⇒ the full pool runs, exactly as today. Adding or
#   narrowing a row only ever ENABLES more skipping; it can never cause an
#   unmapped member to be skipped.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONSERVATIVE-FIRST, NARROW-LATER (PRD §4.1)
#   Seed rows start broad (a closure equivalent to "everything" is always
#   correct — it simply never skips on any real delta). Real merge-time
#   savings come from later narrowing individual rows; an over-broad row is
#   never wrong, only un-optimized. The under-declaration drift-guard
#   (test_run_all_content_skip.sh) is RED if any declared closure omits a
#   repo-relative path token that the member's own source text references.
#
# This file is a LOAD-BEARING verify-pipeline artifact (an edit routes the
# task through the full --scope all gate; see scripts/verify-pipeline-guard.sh).

# --- seed rows (clearly-hermetic pool members; complete closures) -----------
test_portable_sha256.sh scripts/lib_portable.sh
test_portable_mtime.sh scripts/lib_portable.sh tests/infra/test_portable_sha256.sh
test_pycache_gitignored.sh .gitignore
test_gui_dist_gitignored.sh gui/dist .gitignore
